  "body": "## Description\nIn `VotingEscrow` contract, the `delegateBySig()` function incorrectly forbids the delegatee from being the same as the transaction sender (msg.sender):\n```solidity \nrequire(delegatee != msg.sender, \"NA\");\n```\nThis restriction prevents legitimate delegation flows, such as when the intended delegatee relays the delegation transaction on behalf of the delegator. \nBy forbidding `delegatee == msg.sender`, the contract unnecessarily breaks this standard behavior and may prevent user interfaces, wallets, or delegation relayers from functioning properly.\n## Impact\n- Prevents self-delegation.\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\nRemove the restriction:\n```solidity \nrequire(delegatee != msg.sender, \"NA\");\n```",
  "proof_of_concept": "```solidity \nfunction test_submissionValidity() public {\n \n        uint256 pk = 125 ;\n        address alice = vm.addr(pk); // Simulate Alice as the signer\n        address bob = vm.addr(2);   // Alice will delegate to Bob\n        uint nonce = 0;\n        uint expiry = block.timestamp + 1 days;\n        string memory version = \"1.0.0\";\n\n        // Construct the same digest manually according to buggy DOMAIN_TYPEHASH\n        bytes32 DOMAIN_TYPEHASH = keccak256(\"EIP712Domain(string name,uint256 chainId,address verifyingContract)\");\n        bytes32 DELEGATION_TYPEHASH = keccak256(\"Delegation(address delegatee,uint256 nonce,uint256 expiry)\");\n\n        // EIP712 domain (missing `version`)\n        bytes32 domainSeparator = keccak256(\n            abi.encode(\n                DOMAIN_TYPEHASH,\n                keccak256(bytes(votingEscrow.name())),     \n                //keccak256(bytes(version)),\n                block.chainid,\n                address(votingEscrow)\n            )\n        );\n\n        // The actual message struct hash\n        bytes32 structHash = keccak256(\n                        abi.encode(\n                            DELEGATION_TYPEHASH, \n                            bob, \n                            nonce, \n                            expiry\n                        )\n                    );\n\n        bytes32 digest = keccak256(abi.encodePacked(\"\\x19\\x01\", domainSeparator, structHash));\n\n        // Alice Signs message \n        (uint8 v, bytes32 r, bytes32 s) = vm.sign(pk, digest);\n        address signer = ecrecover(digest, v, r, s);\n        assertEq(signer, alice);\n\n        vm.prank(bob);\n        // the call will revert because votingEscrow does allow the delegetee \n        // to be the sender \n        vm.expectRevert();\n        votingEscrow.delegateBySig(bob, nonce, expiry, v, r, s);\n    }\n```",
